Per-residue MM-GBSA decomposition of the 3HFM antibody-antigen interface (episcaf v3, Decision D2).
Single-trajectory MM-GBSA from the existing 20 ns complex trajectory: Coulomb + LJ + GB polar
desolvation + nonpolar. The point is the desolvation term -- it should demote the charged false
positive (Arg73) that raw interaction energy over-called, while keeping the real hot spots
(K96/K97/Y20/D101). Per-residue TOTAL contributions are then compared to SKEMPI alanine ddG with the
same false-positive test (plot_ie_vs_ddg.py, --channel on the MM-GBSA column).

&general
sys_name       = "3HFM",
startframe     = 1,
endframe       = 2000,
interval       = 20,          ; 2000 frames (10 ps each) -> ~100 frames; lower for more sampling
temperature    = 300.0,
/
&gb
igb            = 5,           ; OBC2 generalized Born (standard for MM-GBSA binding)
saltcon        = 0.150,       ; matches the 0.15 M NaCl in the simulation
/
&decomp
idecomp        = 1,           ; per-residue decomposition (TOTAL contribution per residue)
dec_verbose    = 3,           ; print per-residue total (+ backbone/sidechain)
print_res      = "within 5.0" ; decompose residues within 5 A of the partner (the interface)
/
